# Build context for `docker build`. Without this the daemon receives ~790 MB,
# almost all of it .venv, to build a ~10 MB store into an image.
#
# vector_db/ is excluded on purpose: the image ships the runtime export instead
# (see Dockerfile), and leaving it in the context would upload the ablation
# collections the container never opens.
.git
.venv
.env
vector_db/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.github/
corpus/
# `docs/*`, not `docs/` — a re-include cannot reach inside an excluded DIRECTORY,
# because the tool never descends into it. Cloud Build failed on exactly that while a
# local `docker build` let it through, its ignore implementation being looser.
docs/*
!docs/og.png
evaluation/
scripts/
tests/
logs/
uploads/
preprocessed_db/
.DS_Store
